# test: bare_help
# description: Bare amux without a real TTY prints top-level help (on a TTY it
# opens the fleet TUI; scripts and pipes get help, never an alt-screen)

## Environment

terminal:
  name: T1

## Test

@T1
> amux
Terminal multiplexer for AI agents (Claude, Codex, etc.)

Usage: amux [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  ui        Open the fleet TUI (the default when run with no command)
  new       Create a new agent session
  attach    Attach to an existing agent session
  rm        Remove an agent session by exact name or UUID
  list      List running agent sessions, folding child agents into their parent
  keymap    Manage Claude PTY keymaps
  profiles  List profiles through the installation front door
  login     Connect a cloud account, optionally to an explicit profile
  logout    Forget a profile's credential, preserving its device and local agents
  profile   Manage profiles in this installation (select with --profile)
  server    Manage the amux server lifecycle
  init      Initialize local device preferences
  pair      Pair this device with another amux daemon
  peer      Show trusted peers
  unpair    Remove trust for a peer
  update    Update amux to the latest version
  debug     Inspect daemon state and locally captured reports
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>    Path to a profile config file (YAML). Also read from `AMUX_CONFIG`, so managed Claude hooks and daemons spawned by a wrapper find the same instance without adding a config flag to their command [env: AMUX_CONFIG=]
      --profile <PROFILE>  Select a profile by label or UUID
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version

> amux pair --help
Pair this device with another amux daemon

Usage: amux pair [OPTIONS] [TARGET]

Arguments:
  [TARGET]  Host name, IP:port, or user@host to pair through SSH

Options:
      --qr                 Display a QR pairing code for this device
      --link               Also print the QR deep link for simulator pairing
      --listen             Require LAN-direct responder mode; errors when the LAN listener is off
      --demo               Hold a reusable fixed PIN open for unattended demos (returns immediately; the daemon keeps the session until it expires or `amux pair --cancel`)
      --pin <DIGITS>       Six-digit PIN for `--demo`
      --for <DURATION>     How long the `--demo` PIN stays valid, e.g. `30d`, `12h`, `45m`
      --cancel             End any active pairing session on this daemon
      --config <CONFIG>    Path to a profile config file (YAML). Also read from `AMUX_CONFIG`, so managed Claude hooks and daemons spawned by a wrapper find the same instance without adding a config flag to their command [env: AMUX_CONFIG=]
      --profile <PROFILE>  Select a profile by label or UUID
  -h, --help               Print help
